e imaging study</article-title><source>Arch. Gen. Psych.</source><year>2005</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>799</fpage><lpage>805</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blechert</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Michael</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Grossman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lajtman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilhelm</surname><given-names>FH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Autonomic and respiratory characteristics of posttraumatic stress disorder and panic disorder</article-title><source>Psychosom. Med.</source><year>2007</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>935</fpage><lpage>943</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17991823</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bouton</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Mineka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Barlow</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A modern learning theory perspective on the etiology of panic disorder</article-title><source>Psychol. Rev.</source><year>2001</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11212632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000fc;chel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Dolan</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Classical fear conditioning in functional neuroimaging</article-title><source>Curr. Opin. Neurobiol.</source><year>2000</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10753800</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><